  <keyword>psi</keyword>
  <short_description>Digamma and polygamma functions.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Y = psi(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = psi(k, X)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>X</param_name>
      <param_description>a real nonnegative single or double array.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>k</param_name>
      <param_description>order of the derivative: a nonnegative integer scalar.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>Y</param_name>
      <param_description>an array of the size and class of <b>X</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>Y = psi(X)</b> evaluates the digamma function, the logarithmic derivative of the gamma function: <b>psi(x) = gamma'(x) / gamma(x)</b>. <b>psi(0)</b> is <b>-Inf</b>.</p>
    <p><b>Y = psi(k, X)</b> evaluates the polygamma function of order <b>k</b>, the <b>k</b>-th derivative of <b>psi</b>. <b>psi(0, X)</b> is <b>psi(X)</b>.</p>
    <p>Values are computed with the asymptotic expansion after shifting small arguments with the recurrence <b>psi(x + 1) = psi(x) + 1/x</b>.</p>
  </description>
